  "result": {
    "text": "```python\ndef count_nums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Write a function count_nums which takes an array of integers and returns\n    the number of elements which has a sum of digits > 0\n    If If a number is negative, then its first digit will also be negative:\n    e.g. -123 has signed digits -1, 2, and 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for num in arr:\n        if sum(abs(abs(d)) for d in str(abs(num))) > 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\n# Test the function\nimport doctest\n\ndoctest.testmod()\n```\n\n",
